\begin{figure}[t]
  \centering
  \includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figA1_position.pdf}
  \caption{Within-output position as a correctness signal, the same measurement as Table~\ref{tab:rank} with ASQA added. Left: on lists of 5 items or fewer the relationship runs the wrong way, and the usable gradient appears only on longer lists. Right: every ASQA response-length band falls inside $|\rho| < 0.05$, the range where QAMPARI shows no usable signal, and a positive $\rho$ would mean later items are more often correct, the reverse of the direction the method exploits. Both panels use solo assertions only, which removes the support confound, stratified by the asserting agent's own output length. The signal the method depends on is absent at ASQA's response lengths. QAMPARI rows predate the parsing fix of Section~\ref{sec:protocol}.}
  \label{fig:position}
\end{figure}

